# Things that live beside the app but must never be committed.
#
# The application has its own .gitignore inside Whatsapp-CRM/. This one
# covers the repository root, which had none — so every scratch file
# dropped next to the project was one `git add .` away from being
# published, with no warning and no way to take it back.
#
# Nothing listed here has ever been committed. This exists so that stays
# true.

# Working notes. The ones in this repo have held live Meta and Instagram
# access tokens and a 2FA PIN in plain text — the sort of file that is
# genuinely useful to keep locally and catastrophic to push.
/README.txt
/NOTES.txt
/notes.txt

# Browser-automation captures. Accessibility snapshots record whatever
# was on screen, which during a login test is the password and during an
# inbox test is real customers' names, numbers and messages.
.playwright-mcp/
/pw-*.cjs
/pw-*.js

# Exports and backups. Whole-account data, by definition.
/*.zip
/*.tar
/*.tar.gz
/*.sql
/*.dump

# Anything that even looks like credentials.
/.env
/.env.*
/*.pem
/*.key
/*credentials*.json
/*service-account*.json
